e</b>

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
Diet and Nutrition

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
<b>Human Movement Analysis</b>

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
<b>Practical!  Rehabilitation Techniques

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
<b>\h\hScientific Papers
on Running</b>

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
<b>Rehabilitation</b>

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.370
<b>for Broken Legs</b>

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.840
The Kikkashou's in November.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.590
All right!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.590
I'm back!

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.720
T-Teio?!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.460
You're already out of the hospital?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.850
Yeah!

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.360
Well, you're acting like you're fine!

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.610
There goes our peace and quiet.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.060
Oh, please, you were <i>so</i> worried about her!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.810
Teio, I've got it right here.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.520
<b>Perfect Plan
for Tokai Teio's
 Return to Racing
 at the Kikkashou</b>

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.520
The perfect plan for Tokai Teio's 
return to racing at the Kikkashou!{also what the cover sheet says}

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.710
Look at all that!

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.020
Pretty amazing, right?

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.990
What's wrong, guys?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.380
Trainer-san, are you being serious?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.780
I sure am.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.100
If Teio hasn't given up yet, 
I'll do everything I can to support her.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.790
That's what I've decided.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.250
And I'm not giving up!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.080
I'm gonna make my comeback at the Kikkashou!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.490
Make me one promise, though.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.380
What's that?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.880
We'll hang in there until the last minute.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.720
But if the doctor says it's a no-go,
 then you have to give it up.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.530
Okay! I know!

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.680
You scared me! What?!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.900
I'm just so touched right now!

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.730
Teio! I'll help you any way I can!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.350
Coming from you, that's kind of scary.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.240
I want your dream to 
come true, too, Teio-san!

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.860
I'm gonna make it happen. I'll be 
an undefeated Triple Crown winner!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.690
It doesn't seem like there's any 
room for argument, here.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.570
True enough. And if you give up—

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.860
Hang in there, Teio!

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.970
You know I will!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.080
All right, let's get started!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.160
The first step on your path to the Kikkashou!

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.220
It looks like Teio-san's out of the hospital.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.010
Yes. She came to see me 
as soon as she got out.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.920
I'm back, Prez!

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.650
You got out of the hospital quickly.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:52.640
I know, right?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.020
Just watch, Prez! I'll be 
running again in no time!

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.770
That's really something.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.810
It's going to be a battle 
with herself from now on.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.510
Just like what you went through.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.380
Right.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.220
Begin!

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.500
What part of your rehabilitation is this?

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.420
It's called image training.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.460
You're gonna imagine what it's 
like once you're running again.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:25.340
Watch the others run, and always be 
thinking about what you would do!

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.090
If it was me at this speed...

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.220
Once I was in a good position,
I'd hang onto it.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.730
Spe-chan and Gold Ship are both 
great at closing the distance.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:39.120
But with that pressure on me, I'd keep 
my back to them all the way through.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.770
In that case, be sure to get a 
good look at how I run, too.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.150
Although I'm not sure you'll be able 
to keep up, even in your imagination.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:50.320
Trainer-san! I'd like to join in next.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.560
Teio! These used to be mine,
but you can have them.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:56.930
Heavy!

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.500
What are these?

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.460
Weights?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.970
How heavy are the dumbbells you lift, Teio?

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.530
Vodka! That isn't fair, getting ahead of me!

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.850
What does it matter?

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.390
Teio, use this!

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.000
It's important to work on your 
mental health at times like this!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.000
Thanks!

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.680
Teio!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.770
I want you to use this. My S.S. <i>Golshi</i>.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.460
How do you ride it?

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:19.580
You just gotta...

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.010
H-huh?

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:22.440
It's stuck.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.730
Teio-san...

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.340
Maybe it's in a bad mood.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.680
Can I come by your room tonight?

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.860
Come on, work with me here!

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.850
<i>Tips for rehabilitation?</i>

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:34.370
Right, I thought you'd be the 
best person to ask, Suzuka-san.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.370
I'm sorry, Suzuka. I told 
her not to bother, but...

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.250
<i>I'm relieved. You seem to be doing 
better than I worried you might.</i>

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.190
Yeah, same here. Have you lost weight?

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.080
<i>I think so.</i>

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.170
<i>It took me a while to get 
used to the food over here.</i>

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:48.880
Suzuka-san,

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.510
do you want me to send more carrots?!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.640
I've got plenty, thank you.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.930
<i>Teio, congratulations on the Derby.</i>

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.530
Thanks.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:58.010
<i>You're going to try for the Kikkashou?</i>

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:58.580
Yeah.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.840
<i>That's going to make for 
a rough rehab period.</i>

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.120
<i>Are you prepared?</i>

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:03.900
Yeah!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.300
<i>The most important thing is 
to not push yourself too hard.</i>

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.290
<i>If you rush it, you could 
end up injuring yourself again.</i>

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:14.160
Our Trainer said the same thing.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.630
But there's so little time...

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.750
<i>I know. And I understand how you feel.</i>

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>But getting plenty of rest is 
an important part of rehab.</i>

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.090
<i>And there are things you can 
do while you're resting, too.</i>

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:31.950
Teio...

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.180
What the hell is she doing?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.390
Research.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.690
Research?!

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.600
Suzuka-san gave her some advice yesterday.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.600
<b>Winning Data for Every Race
 The Racing Textbook
 Racing Theory for the Committed 
 Everything There Is To Learn About Turf</b>

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.630
All right, I've got some stuff to teach her!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.230
It's a bad idea to try make your move right

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.820
before the third corner of
the outer track in Kyoto!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.000
Aw, would you keep it down?

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.820
Got that? No matter what!

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.010
That last race was a close one.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:52.820
Hey...

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:57.330
What would you say if I told you I was 
thinking about entering the Kikkashou?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.990
Kikkashou?! G-1?!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.800
It probably wouldn't work... right?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.810
I wanna enter, too!

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.420
Turbo-san, you'd need to win more first.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.220
Then I will!

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:05.540
I'll totally win the next race!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:09.330
If I can keep coming in first place 
with the next few races, can I manage?

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.960
Give me just a second.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.580
You're feeling fired up, 
huh, Nature? How come?

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.180
Teio might still be running in it.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.810
Tokai Teio?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.920
But she's...

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.480
She hasn't given up.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:27.320
So... I might not be up for it, but...

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.570
If I win this, this, and the Kokura Kinen...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.920
Will I be able to enter?

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.320
Uh, yes.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.490
Let's get cracking on some training, then!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.850
Okay, I'm gonna give this a try!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:41.500
<b>Aim for a G1 Win!</b>

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.960
You can do it, Teio!

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:44.350
I watch all your races!

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.510
What?

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.770
What? What?!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.650
What, what, what?! What the heck?

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:05.660
What is all this?!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.110
You want to be ready in time 
for the Kikkashou, right?

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:11.640
This is the Mejiro family physical therapist.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.030
I'm the physical therapist.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:14.230
Acupuncturist.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.700
I'm the acupuncturist.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.450
Chef.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.410
I'm the chef.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.440
Patissier.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.780
I'm the patissier.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.920
You are welcome to spend the weekend

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.720
relaxing here at the estate 
in luxury, Teio-sama.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:29.500
O-Okay... McQueen, what's going on?

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.670
I thought it'd be a good idea 
to use every resource available.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.650
The family physician is also available.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.070
That's me.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:43.140
Why do you have that needle?!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.930
Because I am the young lady's family doctor.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.420
That doesn't explain anything!

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.230
I'll be taking my leave, then.

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:50.970
If there's anything you're 
unclear on, let me know.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.280
I just <i>said</i> I don't get what's going on!

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.990
McQueen... don't abandon me... please...

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.990
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.990
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:06.750
The cast is off!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.610
I won't have to wear the 
brace for long, either.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.090
This is where it gets serious. Got it?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.760
Sweets! Sweets! Sweets!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.640
You wanna run, Teio?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.520
Of course I do!

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.130
Well, hold back!

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.050
Take that desire to run 
and convert it to energy!

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:35.390
You're gonna need to teach your 
leg again that it's a runner's leg!

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:36.780
Yeah!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.200
Stay focused, Spe.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.670
I just keep wondering how she's doing.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:49.400
The only thing we can really do for 
Teio is to show her our backs as we run.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.080
Right!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.170
Nicely put, McQueen!

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.680
And with that being the case...

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:54.840
Hey, no fair!

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.140
I'm going, too!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.150
You wanna take me on?!

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.280
I won't be outdone!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.200
Argh, I wanna run, too!

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.150
That's the spirit! Don't forget that feeling!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.090
May I sit here?

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.620
Sure!

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:41.850
How are you doing?

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.270
Right on schedule! What else did you expect?

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.970
You really are something, Teio.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.220
You seem to be doing well, too, Nature.
 You're on a three-win streak.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.470
I guess I am.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:51.890
Pardon me.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.340
Hey, you came.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.400
Nature, who's this?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.860
Canopus has another new member.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.750
I'm Ikuno Dictus.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:01.590
<b>I
k
u
n
o
 
D
i
c
t
u
s</b>

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.160
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.760
N-Nice to meet you!

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:06.660
Canopus is aiming to become 
the school's foremost team.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.720
We are?

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:11.160
Were you not the one who suggested 
we aim high, Nature-san?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.750
I guess so!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.260
I think I remember saying that.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:15.380
It's all right.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.480
If we execute my plan, it's possible 
for us to achieve that goal.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.270
What we need in order to accomplish that 
is an overwhelming amount of experience.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:26.040
As well as the robust physicality 
and steely mentality

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.040
I guess your team's got 
another interesting new girl.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.140
I guess.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.490
necessary to withstand such rigorous rotation.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.490
Anyway, Teio...

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:31.650
I'm fully aware that it won't be a 
simple task to achieve these things.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:31.650
I'm going to be entering the trials.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.230
But I believe that a single tangible experience

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:34.490
And if I win there, I'll 
be racing in the Kikkashou.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.780
is more valuable than 
100 theoretical situations.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.430
And no experience is more valuable than racing.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.140
I'll be waiting.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:37.580
It is all about racing.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:39.860
Because it's my dream to beat you.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.430
Which is to say that in 
training to race,

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.050
races themselves are a 
part of your training.

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:42.400
There is a school of thought that says

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:42.610
Right!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.810
to train like you're in 
the actual competition.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:45.610
Thus, by all means...

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.620
<b>October</b>

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.620
